            "is_markdown": true,
            "bug_id": 19340,
            "text": "## Summary\n\nIn a UTF-8 locale, `text()` on a `pdf()` or `postscript()` device reads past the end of a string that ends part way through a UTF-8 character, and on Windows also of one holding a byte from 0xF8 that `iconv()` cannot convert. Fixes a reproducible segfault: an out-of-bounds read reachable from plain R code (an error on Linux and macOS, a crash on Windows).\n\n## Details\n\nWhen `iconv()` fails on a character, `mbcsToSbcs()` in `src/library/grDevices/src/devPS.c` decodes it with `utf8toucs()` and steps over `utf8clen()` bytes. It treats only `-1` as an error, but `utf8toucs()` also returns `-2`, for a truncated sequence and, on Windows, for any lead byte from 0xF8; the step then passes the terminator and the next `iconv()` reads far beyond the string (ASan: negative-size-param). Since r85256 (R 4.4.0); seen in R-devel r90926 and R 4.6.1, patch tested on Linux, macOS and Windows.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `devps-truncated-utf8-repro.R`; runs four strings in fresh R processes: three fail before the patch (on Windows all four, three as segfaults), none after.\n\nProposed patch: attached as `devps-truncated-utf8.diff`; tests for `res > 0`, so these get one dot per byte, and adds a test to `grDevices/tests/encodings.R`.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/512, where CI results can be seen."
